{
  "about": "Cost of every recorded KIBO Learn run (scripts/learn-cost.ts, `npm run learn:cost`, checked by scripts/learn-cost.test.ts): tokens from each run's learn-stats.json x the gemini-3.8-flash prices below, USD rounded to 4 decimals. Uncached input at flashInput, cached input at flashCachedInput, output at flashOutput. The learner called gemini-3.8-flash on Vertex AI, while these are the Gemini API's paid-tier list prices; the Vertex AI price for this model was not read (unverified). Thinking tokens are not recorded: the learner sums usageMetadata promptTokenCount, cachedContentTokenCount and candidatesTokenCount only (spikes/kibo-learn/learner.mjs) and sets no thinking config, so outputTokens does not include thoughtsTokenCount and these costs leave thinking out (output is a lower bound). `cachedRecorded: false` (a learner before 13-blind-kiosks:4, which wrote 0 for cached tokens) bills all input as uncached (input is an upper bound). `finished` is the learner's own flag (the finish gate passed and a skill was written); `skillWritten` is whether skill.json is in the run folder. Groups are kept apart on purpose: they used different learners on kiosks with different histories, so there is no combined total. `totals` sum every run in a group, including attempts the docs do not report as the result (`reported: false`); `totalsReportedRunsOnly` leaves those out. Read each group's note and each run's label before quoting a number.",
